{{also|antedaté}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|ante|date}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæntiˌdeɪt/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-antedate.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To occur before an event or [[time]]; to exist further back in time.
#: {{syn|en|predate|Thesaurus:predate}}
#: {{ant|en|postdate}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1931|author=[[w:H. P. Lovecraft|H[oward] P[hillips] Lovecraft]]|title=w:The Whisperer in Darkness|chapter=2|passage=I suppose you know all about the fearful myths '''antedating''' the coming of man to the earth—the Yog-Sothoth and Cthulhu cycles—which are hinted at in the ''Necronomicon''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1986|title=People v. Calio|url=https://law.justia.com/cases/california/supreme-court/3d/42/639.html|others=42 Cal.3d 639,644|passage=We therefore turn to the question whether defendant's prior convictions for burglary and attempted burglary could be used as the basis for an enhancement under [California Penal Code] sections 667 and 1192.7. Both prior convictions '''antedate''' the effective date of section 667.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Giancarlo Gandolfo|title=Economic Dynamics|edition=4th|publisher=Springer|page=311
|passage=Actually, mathematical models of multi-sector growth models '''antedate''' the Harrod-Domar and Solow-Swan aggregate models.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2024|author=Jeremy Bay Rudd|title=A Practical Guide to Macroeconomics|publisher=Cambridge University Press|page=281|passage=
Dimensional analysis is a serious business in the natural sciences, where what you're measuring actually exists  [&hellip;]; and it even has a theorem that goes with it (Buckingham's <math>\pi</math> theorem, which like any good mathematical theorem with a name attached, apparently '''antedates''' Buckingham).
}}
# To assign a date to a document or action earlier than the actual date.
#: {{syn|en|backdate|foredate|Thesaurus:backdate}}
#: {{ant|en|postdate|overdate|Thesaurus:overdate}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1633|author=John Donne|title=Woman's Constancy|passage=Tomorrow when you leav’st, what wilt thou say? / Wilt thou then '''antedate''' some new-made vow?}}
# {{lb|en|lexicography}} To find earlier [[citational]] evidence for a term.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=James Lambert|title=A multitude of “lishes”: The nomenclature of hybridity|work=English World-Wide|year=2017|month=January|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318367113_A_multitude_of_lishes_The_nomenclature_of_hybridity|volume=38|issue=3|issn=0172-8865|doi=10.1075/eww.38.3.04lam|text=Furthermore, while ''OED'' entries are generally regarded as a good indication of when terms were first used in English, for 5 of the 7 terms the present research has been able to '''antedate''' ''OED''’s earliest attestations, usually by a decade or more.}}

